ARTEMIS is a DNA repair enzyme that plays a critical role in regulating V(D)J recombination. This process is essential for the development of functional T and B cells, which are critical components of the immune system. By facilitating error-prone DNA repair, ARTEMIS ensures the proper rearrangement of gene segments in these cells, which leads to the production of diverse antibodies and T cell receptors. Without ARTEMIS, T and B cells would not function properly, resulting in defective immune responses.  

Thus, ARTEMIS is indispensable for maintaining the diversity of immune responses needed to combat a wide range of pathogens.  

\boxed{ARTEMIS ensures error-prone DNA repair during V(D)J recombination, which enables the production of diverse antibodies and T cell receptors. This is critical for functional immune responses.}

